{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "John Meets Sandra"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "How Did It Go?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le07ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Agreeing and Disagreeing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use different phrases to agree and disagree tactfully (politely).<br/> Generally, you use the Simple Present Tense in the affirmative to agree. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Don't you think coconut water is good for your body?</br><span class=\"strong\">Sandra</span>: Absolutely."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sandra</span>: Coffee isn't healthy for you.</br> <span class=\"strong\">John</span>: That's not always true."}, {"type": "text", "content": "At the workplace, we ask for others' opinion with questions such as:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>What do you think?</li> <li>I'm interested in your feedback/input.</li> <li>Please let me know your thoughts.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We show agreement or disagreement with statements in the chart below."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Agreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disagreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I agree with you 100 percent.</br> I couldn't agree with you more.</br> That's so true.</br> You're absolutely right.</br> Absolutely.</br> That's exactly how I feel.</br> Exactly.</br> You have a point there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't think so.</br> I'm afraid I disagree.</br> I beg to differ.</br> Not necessarily.</br> That's not always true.</br> I'm not sure if ...</br> I see what you're saying, but ...</br> I don't know about that ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives & Superlatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use adjectives to compare two things. These are called <span class=\"strong\">comparative</span> adjectives. You can also use adjectives to compare one item with the rest of a group. These are called <span class=\"strong\">superlative</span> adjectives."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Selling good quality products is <span class=\"underline\">as</span> important <span class=\"underline\">as</span> good customer service."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are <span class=\"underline\">more</span> people at this workshop <span class=\"underline\">than</span> the last one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There were <span class=\"underline\">less</span> people at the last workshop <span class=\"underline\">than</span> this one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For comparative adjectives, you can use the structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">as</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">as</span> </br>adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-er</span>) <span class=\"strong\">than</span></br> <span class=\"strong\">more/less</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">than</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives with 3 syllables or more use <span class=\"strong italic\">more/less</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"strong italic\">than</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For superlative adjectives, you can use:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> <li>adjective  (<span class=\"strong\">-est</span>)</li> <li><span class=\"strong\">most/least</span> + adjective</li> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives with 3 syllables or more use <span class=\"strong italic\">most/least</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The adjectives <span class=\"italic\">good</span> and <span class=\"italic\">bad</span> are irregular adjectives. They do not follow the same rules."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Good ----> better-----> best</br> Bad -----> worse -----> worst"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to participate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to join in an activity or event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's important that all employees participate in this workshop."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to register"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put your name in to join an activity or event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must register for the workshop before attending."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "let me know your thoughts"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ideas or opinions a person is thinking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let me know your thoughts on the new system at work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to demonstrate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show with action how to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sandra demonstrated how to do a good presentation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "electronic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "used with a computer or the internet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An electronic reservation system would be easier and faster than a paper system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to establish"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put a system or relationship firmly in place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sandra established a good relationship with her clients."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rapport"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "good friendly relations with others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a good idea to have a good rapport with all your customers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le07ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences on how you bought movie tickets or train tickets 10 years ago. Use past tense verbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences comparing this old system to how you buy these tickets now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner your opinion and ask for their opinion on the two systems."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements on things I did in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make comparisons between old and new procedures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I tell others my opinion and ask others for their opinion."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le07ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le07ob09re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "John receives an e-mail from his boss, Mr. Micklewhite:</br><br/>\n<span class=\"italic\">micklewhite@cruisemail.com wrote:</span></br>\nHello, John. I understand you participated in the workshop on customer service last week. There were more people than in other past workshops. I'm interested in your feedback on it. I think more tour guides should register. Please let me know your thoughts.", "id": 1, "time": "10", "image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"italic\">John.Harris@mail.com wrote:</span></br></br>\nHello, Mr. Micklewhite. The workshop was really helpful for me. I certainly agree more guides would find it useful. However, I'm not sure if every guide will have time to attend. Sandra did a fantastic job. I learned about more efficient reservation procedures.", "id": 2, "time": "18000", "image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "Sandra demonstrated how an electronic system is faster than a paper and pen system. She also established a good rapport with the group. It was the best workshop ever on this ship. I hope future workshops will be as interesting as this was.", "id": 3, "time": "35000", "image": "engenn5le07ob09re2img08.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can agree and disagree tactfully."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can make comparisons."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Tell your friend about your favorite movie. Ask them what they think."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you agree or disagree with them?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Compare your favorite movie with your partner's."}]}, {"type